Represent type parameters without a universe

Extend contexts by fresh types so polymorphic declarations do not need
type codes, decoding, or a universe. Keep type arguments separate from
term arguments throughout elaboration, substitution, and constructor
computation. Restrict Type to parameter binders, excluding type-valued
definitions and equality between types.

Infer equality formation from its endpoints and give reflexivity a term
argument. Record weakening maps in extension requests and use native
identity morphisms. Retain checked formation and substitution requests
because allocated syntax must not establish its own typing judgments.

Exercise polymorphic definitions, indexed families, fresh type contexts,
deferred checking, and invalid arguments in the evaluator integration
suite, and document the reasons for the remaining kernel machinery.
